      "problem": "If $\\overset{―}{S}={p,q,r,x,y,z}$ and $\\overset{―}{T}={q,v,z},$ then what is $\\overset{―}{S\\cup T}?$",
      "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for unions states that\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{S\\cup T}≡\\overset{―}{S}\\cap \\overset{―}{T}.\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{S\\cup T} & =\\overset{―}{S}\\cap \\overset{―}{T} \\\\  & ={p,q,r,x,y,z}\\cap {q,v,z} \\\\  & ={q,z}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
